  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d5562cc34807e2439c5cc188b7351d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC2_IntroDialog
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogSequence
  lines:
  - speakerName: Guide
    text: "Alright, welcome to Networking 101! Before this PC can talk to anything
      else, it needs a proper network cable \u2014 and you're going to make one from
      scratch."
  - speakerName: Guide
    text: 'You''ll find a crimping station nearby. That''s where the real work happens:
      stripping, arranging, and crimping an RJ45 connector onto a length of cable.'
  - speakerName: Guide
    text: "Cable wiring isn't random \u2014 it follows a standard called TIA/EIA-568,
      so each of the 8 wires has an exact spot it needs to go. Get the order wrong,
      and the cable simply won't work."
  - speakerName: Guide
    text: Head over to the crimping station and grab the tool. I'll walk you through
      the color order once you're there.
